<item><title>Supply and Installation of Structured Cabling &amp; Related Physical Network Infrastructure</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Services for design, install, test, certify, and warranty of structured copper and fibre cabling infrastructure—along with the necessary physical infrastructure (cabinets, racks, pathways, and UPS equipment)—across Massey’s three campuses. Delivery of these services must conform to strict technical standards and documentation requirements provided by Massey.<br /><br />The outcome of the procurement is to identify a preferred supplier who can provide the services outlined above at each of the Massey campuses – Auckland, Manawatu, and Wellington.<br /><br />It is further expected that the supplier will also undertake additional tasks required to support the network upgrade programme – such as physically installing wireless access points (APs) and network switches (mounting in ceilings or racks), installing and connecting UPS units, decommissioning old cabling or hardware, and performing cable fault-finding/repair services as needed. (Note: Ongoing maintenance of active network devices is excluded from this cab...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Massey University<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 11/Nov/2026 12:00 pm (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2700<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.nz/tsi.axd?id=f4cdf976faae41f08913e776ebf90bd1s2700s930449e3ff934542b58ea67687191124s70</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">f4cdf976faae41f08913e776ebf90bd1</guid>
<pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:53:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>IT &amp; Telecomms</category>
</item>
<item><title>High Street Water Main Upgrade</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> 2.2	Indicative Scope of Physical Works<br /><br />The following comprises the proposed project scope. Note that this may be subject to some changes and refinement resulting from the ECI process and ongoing design works. See Figure 1 below for a visual representation of the scope (preliminary concept plan). <br /><br />Water Main <br /><br />•	Upgrade the existing DN200 water main between King Street and the Railway Drain to a new DN300 water.<br /><br />•	Renew all adjoining connecting pipes connected to the existing DN200 water main within the High Street corridor, generally on a like-for-like diameter where the mean renewal dates fall within the next 10 years. This includes: <br /><br />?	Replacement of approximately 14m of DN100 PVC (1989 install) (Asset: 170780) extending south of the High/King Street roundabout.<br /><br />?	Replacement of DN100 AC (1981 install) (Asset: 170781) servicing 215 High Street, up to the boundary with an isolation valve at the boundary<br /><br />?	Replacement of appx. 13m of ...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Waimakariri District Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 04/Nov/2026 04:00 pm (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2699<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
